    Bind START_JOB metadata to deployed metadata (#4818)
    
    ## What
    
    Bind client START_JOB launch metadata to the deployed job metadata
    before selecting a job launcher.
    
    The client now reads the deployed `meta.json` and rejects START_JOB
    metadata drift for launch/runtime-sensitive fields:
    
    - `job_id`
    - `resource_spec`
    - `launcher_spec`
    - `scope`
    - `study`
    
    Scheduler-maintained start metadata such as status and participating
    clients can still be recorded.
    
    ## Why
    
    Deploy-time app authorization and metadata verification happen before
    the client writes the deployed `meta.json`. START_JOB previously
    accepted fresh `job_meta` from the server, rewrote local metadata with
    it, and selected Docker/K8s launch settings from that start-time
    metadata. A tampered START_JOB could therefore replace
    image/resource/study/scope metadata after deploy.
